  "purpose": "probe_families answered the diff-of-means-only caveat for eight LINEAR families, which leaves exactly one cheap objection against the saturation result and the affordance inversion: that a non-linear probe would have been informative where every linear one was not. This runs the identical protocol - same splits, same layer selection, same null pairs, same concealment test - for two non-linear families: a one-hidden-layer MLP trained with weight decay and early data standardisation, and a k-nearest-neighbour scorer with cosine distance, which is as non-parametric as a probe gets. Neither produces a direction; both produce scores, which is all AUROC needs. If both saturate the paraphrase null, the regime claim extends beyond linearity. If either separates concealed from disclosed steering, that family refutes the inversion and is the probe this project should have used.",
